# Own-wording Tome of Heroes spells, chunk B (Calm Beasts to Ethereal Stairs). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Calm Beasts": "You try to soothe angry or frightened animals. Each beast in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you choose within range makes a Charisma saving throw. For each that fails, pick one effect. Suppress any effect making the target Charmed or Frightened, and the suppressed effect resumes when the spell ends if its duration has not run out. Or make the target indifferent to creatures of your choice that it is hostile toward. This ends if the target is attacked, harmed by a spell, or sees an ally harmed. When the spell ends the creature turns hostile again unless the GM rules otherwise.",
"Clear the Board": "You send allies and enemies to opposite sides of the field. Pick a cardinal direction. You and up to five willing friendly creatures within range teleport up to 90 feet that way to spaces you can see. Up to six hostile creatures within range make a Wisdom saving throw, and each that fails is teleported up to 90 feet in the opposite direction, to spaces you can see. You cannot teleport a target into hazards such as lava or off a cliff edge, and each target lands in a free space on the ground or a floor.",
"Conjure Construct": "You summon a construct of Challenge Rating 5 or lower to harry your foes. It appears in a free space you can see within range and disappears when it drops to 0 hit points or the spell ends. It is friendly to you and your companions, rolls its own Initiative and takes its own turns. It obeys your verbal commands with no action from you, and if you give none it defends itself but takes no other actions. If your Concentration breaks, the construct stays but turns hostile to you and your companions and may attack. You cannot dismiss an uncontrolled construct, and it disappears 1 hour after you summoned it. It deals double damage to objects and structures. The GM has its statistics.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The Challenge Rating rises by 1 for each slot level above 5th.",
"Conjure Spectral Allies": "You scatter graveyard dirt and call vengeful spirits, which erupt from the ground at a point you choose within range and sweep outward. Each creature in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on that point makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure it takes 6d10 Necrotic damage and is Frightened for 1 minute. On a success it takes half damage and is not Frightened. A creature Frightened this way repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 7th.",
"Convey Inner Peace": "You and up to five willing creatures within range gain the ability to enter an elf-like meditative trance. Once before the spell ends, an affected creature can finish a rest in 4 hours by meditating as an elf does, and gains the same benefit it would from 8 hours of rest.",
"Crown of Thorns": "You bind the mind of a creature within range. Until the spell ends, each time it casts a spell it makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failure it takes 2d6 Psychic damage and the casting fails, and no spell slot is spent.",
"Damaging Intel": "You study a creature you can see within range to learn its weaknesses. It makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failure you learn its damage vulnerabilities, resistances and immunities, and the next attack an ally in range makes against it before the end of your next turn has Advantage.",
"Dead Walking": "You place a copper piece under your tongue as you cast. Up to six willing creatures you can see within range become invisible to undead for the duration, along with anything they wear or carry. The spell ends for all targets if one of them attacks or casts a spell.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot, it lasts 1 hour with no Concentration. With a slot of 4th level or higher, the duration also increases by 1 hour for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Deadly Salvo": "Ammunition flies from your hand with a loud bang, aimed at up to five creatures or objects you can see within range, at one target or several. Make a ranged spell attack for each bullet. On a hit the target takes 3d6 Piercing damage. This damage can Gunpowder Burst, but the spell counts as a single effect for how many times the damage can burst, no matter how many targets.",
"Devouring Darkness": "Choose up to six points you can see within range. Void-like magical darkness fills a 10-foot-radius sphere around each one for the duration, spreading around corners. Darkvision cannot see through it, and no light can illuminate it. Each creature inside a sphere when you cast the spell makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure it takes 6d10 Piercing and 5d6 Psychic damage and is Restrained by unseen entities biting and tearing from the Void. On a success it takes half damage and is not Restrained. A Restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC, ending the condition on a success. When a creature enters a sphere for the first time on a turn or starts its turn in one, it makes an Intelligence saving throw, taking 5d6 Psychic damage on a failure or half on a success. The spheres cannot move. A creature in overlapping spheres suffers no extra effect.",
"Dimensional Shove": "You push a creature you touch through a dimensional portal. If it fails a Wisdom saving throw, it vanishes and reappears 30 feet from you in a direction you choose. The trip can pass through walls, creatures and other solids, but it cannot end inside a solid object or off solid ground. Otherwise it appears in the nearest safe free space along the path.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The target is shoved an extra 30 feet for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Divine Retribution": "With a last word before you fall unconscious, you inflict Radiant damage on your attacker equal to 1d8 + the damage you took from the triggering attack. A fiend or undead takes an extra 1d8 Radiant damage. The attacker then makes a Constitution saving throw or is Stunned for 1 minute. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the Stun on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 1st.",
"Door of the Far Traveler": "You conjure a door to a destination of your choice that lasts for the duration or until dispelled. Draw the outline of a door in chalk on any hard surface (a wall, cliff, ship deck) and scribe sigils of power around it. The door must be at least 1 foot wide and 2 feet tall, and no larger than 5 feet wide and 10 feet tall. Place the knob, which attaches magically, and your drawing becomes a real door to the destination. Anyone can open it, close it and pass through in either direction. The destination can be on any plane and must be familiar to you. How familiar decides accuracy, as the GM determines. A place you have visited is 100 percent accurate. A place only described to you by someone who was there may put you in the wrong room or structure. Third-hand knowledge may put you in a similar structure in a very different place. The spell creates no doorway at the destination. It links to an existing, working door, so it cannot open onto a bare field or forest without a doorframe built for the purpose. While active, that existing doorway connects only to the area you occupied when casting. If you link to a doorway between a parlor and library and your door opens into the library, people can still walk from parlor to library normally, but anyone going the other way arrives where you came from. Before casting, spend 1 hour etching symbols on the knob, the material component, to attune it to your destination. It stays attuned until used or until you spend another hour attuning it elsewhere. Removing the knob from the door dispels the spell, and you can do so as a bonus action from either side when the door is shut. If the duration expires naturally, the knob falls to the ground on your side. When the spell ends the knob loses its attunement.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 9th-level slot, the duration is 12 hours.",
"Dreamwine": "You imbue a bottle of wine with fey magic. During the casting, you and up to seven other creatures drink it. When casting finishes, each drinker can see invisible creatures and objects as if visible, can see into the Ethereal Plane, and has Advantage on Charisma checks and saves for the duration. Ethereal creatures and objects look ghostly and translucent.",
"Emerald Eyes": "You try to drive a creature you can see within range into a paranoid, murderous rage. It makes a Wisdom saving throw or becomes convinced those around it want to steal everything it has, from its job to its loved ones' affection to its wealth, however trusted they are and however absurd the theft. While affected, it must use its action to attack the nearest creature other than itself or you. If it starts its turn with no creature near enough to reach and attack, it repeats the save, and on a success it acts freely that turn. If that happens a second time, it repeats the save again and on a success the spell ends. Each time it takes damage it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 3rd, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Enchanted Bloom": "You spend an hour anointing a rose with scented oils and imbuing it with fey magic. The first creature other than you that touches the rose before the spell ends pricks itself and makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failure it falls into a deep slumber for 24 hours, which only greater restoration or similar magic breaks, or you ending the spell as an action. While asleep it needs no food or drink and does not age. Each time it takes damage it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The slumber lasts 7 days with a 6th-level slot, 30 days with 7th, 180 days with 8th and a year with 9th.",
"Eruption": "You create a raging volcano centered on a point you can see within range. A cinder cone 2 feet wide and 5 feet tall bursts from the ground. Each creature within 30 feet of it makes a Strength saving throw, taking 8d6 Bludgeoning damage and being knocked Prone on a failure, or half damage and not Prone on a success. While you concentrate, it grows each round on your turn.\n\nRound 2: smoke pours out. Each creature within 10 feet takes 4d6 Poison damage. Afterward a creature that enters the smoke for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there takes 2d6 Poison damage. The smoke spreads around corners and heavily obscures its area. Moderate wind (10 mph) disperses it until your next turn, when it reforms.\nRound 3: lava covers the ground within 20 feet of the cone. Each creature and object there takes 10d10 Fire damage and catches fire. Afterward, a creature that enters the lava for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there takes 5d10 Fire damage. The smoke now fills a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on the cone.\nRound 4: the lava covers the ground within 30 feet to a depth of 1 foot, making it difficult terrain, and the smoke fills a 30-foot-radius sphere.\nRound 5: the lava reaches 40 feet and the smoke a 40-foot radius. The cone spews hot rocks. Choose up to three creatures within 90 feet of it, each making a Dexterity saving throw or taking 3d6 Bludgeoning and 3d6 Fire damage.\nRounds 6 to 10: lava and smoke each grow 10 feet per round, and each round you can have the cone spew hot rocks at three targets as in Round 5.\n\nWhen the spell ends, the eruption stops but the smoke and lava remain for 1 minute before cooling and dispersing. The landscape is permanently altered.",
"Ethereal Stairs": "You create a staircase from thin air. A shimmering staircase 10 feet wide appears for the duration, climbing at 45 degrees to a point up to 60 feet above the ground. Only the steps are solid, with no apparent support unless you make it look like stone or wood. Its magical nature stays obvious, since it is colorless and translucent, and the rest of it is no more solid than air. It supports up to 10 tons. It can be straight, spiral or switchback. Its bottom must touch solid ground, but its top need not touch anything.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The staircase extends 20 feet more for each slot level above 5th.",
}
